Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:37:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] GR00T_N17 processor: build PIL images with cv2.merge

Image.fromarray on a transposed CHW->HWC view makes PIL copy it through a slow
strided tobytes (~1.4 ms per 256x256 image, ~4 ms per sample). cv2.merge builds the
same HWC array ~20x faster. Pixels are identical (seeded before/after comparison of
processed samples and collated batches).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../gr00t/model/gr00t_n1d7/processing_gr00t_n1d7.py      | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/policy/GR00T_N17/gr00t_n17/gr00t/model/gr00t_n1d7/processing_gr00t_n1d7.py b/policy/GR00T_N17/gr00t_n17/gr00t/model/gr00t_n1d7/processing_gr00t_n1d7.py
index 30155dc..bf5f4f8 100644
--- a/policy/GR00T_N17/gr00t_n17/gr00t/model/gr00t_n1d7/processing_gr00t_n1d7.py
+++ b/policy/GR00T_N17/gr00t_n17/gr00t/model/gr00t_n1d7/processing_gr00t_n1d7.py
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ from typing import Any, Dict
 import warnings
 
 import albumentations as A
+import cv2
 import numpy as np
 from PIL import Image
 import torch
@@ -454,8 +455,12 @@ class Gr00tN1d7Processor(BaseProcessor):
                 video: [T, C, H, W]
         Returns: vlm_content format for collation
         """
-        # Convert images to PIL format
-        pil_images = [Image.fromarray(np.transpose(v, (1, 2, 0))) for v in images]
+        # Convert images to PIL format. cv2.merge builds the HWC array ~20x faster than PIL
+        # copying a transposed view; the pixels are identical.
+        pil_images = [
+            Image.fromarray(cv2.merge(list(v)) if v.shape[0] > 1 else np.transpose(v, (1, 2, 0)))
+            for v in images
+        ]
 
         # Create conversation with images and text
         conversation = [
